{% lede %}
Around 2013 I drew four display typefaces in Illustrator. Each one starts from a single idea about letter shape and carries it through a full alphabet.
{% /lede %}

Edgar is sharp and angular, with a blackletter accent. Edgar's Dream is rounder and heavier. Wonder goes the other way: thin, monoline and curling. The last face carves each letter out of a solid block.

Designing a whole alphabet is a lesson in consistency. A rule that looks good on one letter has to survive all 26, uppercase and lowercase, and still read as one family.
